TI  - RESTful Web Service Implementation on Unklab Information System Using JSON Web Token (JWT)
T2  - PROCEEDINGS OF ICORIS 2020: 2020 THE 2ND INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON CYBERNETICS AND INTELLIGENT SYSTEM (ICORIS)
CP  - 2nd International Conference on Cybernetics and Intelligent System (ICORIS)
KW  - Student data
KW  - RESTful Web Service
KW  - Information System
KW  - JSON Web Token
KW  - API
AB  - Student data that are public and stored on Universitas Klabat currently be stored in a local database and can only be accessed by the database administrator. A RESTful web service acts as a medium that provides access to the data for those who have permission, improving the data's accessibility. Any user eligible by the web service can use the Universitas Klabat Information System data to develop a mobile or another web application without making another similar database, thus eliminating the redundant process of making a duplicate database. A JSON Web Token is also used in this web service to ensure that the person accessing the web service is authorized to access the specific data. The agile method is used to develop this application. In conclusion, the web service can create, read, update, delete operation regarding the student database and provide it to the user that is authorized with a valid JSON Web Token.
