AB  - Cloud computing is a cutting-edge technology that integrates a variety of networked devices to provide required services. Individuals as well as organizations can use cloud computing to gain on-demand access to handled and scalable IT resources such as servers, storage, and apps via a shared network.. However, in such systems, a large user base from many fields, each with their own set of policies, can lead to a variety of issues, such as the loss of access control information, theft, or unauthorized use of information. To overcome these issues, researchers and specialists have developed a number of approaches for ensuring secure access to cloud services. This essay compares and summarizes access control models.To overcome the drawbacks of existing models, we propose a more effective and sophisticated extended access control model based on chaotic systems.
