CP  - 2nd International Conference on Telematics and Future Generation Networks (TAFGEN)
KW  - Cloud computing
KW  - access control model
KW  - data security
AB  - Cloud computing has emerged as a de-facto standard that aims at delivering computing as a service. Due to significant ease of access advantages using cloud computing, organizations stored their sensitive data into cloud storage, which brings data security and privacy challenges. Access Control methods implemented in cloud need to balance the ease of user access while safeguarding against unauthorized access. In this paper, we will explain cloud computing infrastructure, the corresponding data security threats in clouds and review Role-based Access Control model from existing literature which only support for cross domain authentication.
