TI  - PDPChain: A Consortium Blockchain-Based Privacy Protection Scheme for Personal Data
T2  - IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON RELIABILITY
KW  - Blockchains
KW  - Access control
KW  - Data privacy
KW  - Cryptography
KW  - Homomorphic encryption
KW  - Authentication
KW  - Cloud computing
KW  - Consortium blockchain
KW  - ciphertext policy attribute-based encryption (CP-ABE)
KW  - homomorphic encryption
KW  - InterPlanetary File System (IPFS)
KW  - privacy protection
KW  - secure sharing
AB  - With the advances and innovations in digital technologies, blockchain has empowered advancements in communications and networking, promising to build trust and establish secure decentralized communications networks. Unfortunately, current personal data privacy protection schemes still suffer from explicit storage, lack of data ownership and implementation of fine-grained access control by users, and lack of transparency and auditability of data. In this article, we propose a personal data privacy protection scheme based on consortium blockchain that stores original data encrypted with an improved Paillier homomorphic encryption mechanism, namely PDPChain, where users realize fine-grained access control based on ciphertext policy attribute-based encryption (CP-ABE) on blockchain. In this scheme, consortium blockchain combines distributed private clusters to store the encrypted data, improving data transmission efficiency, and guaranteeing user privacy and security through off-chain storage and on-chain transmission synergy. In addition, it is more lightweight encryption and demarcation, ultimately protecting personal data privacy and providing a secure and trusted way to obtain information for data mining. For the performance testing, data in the form of files are used as an example, and the scheme is designed and simulated on Hyperledger Fabric and InterPlanetary File System. Experimental results show that the improved Paillier encryption mechanism reduces the overall encryption and decryption elapsed time by 25% and encryption elapsed time by 48%. Furthermore, the proposed CP-ABE access control method is adaptive to storing and sharing a massive amount of data. With the increase in the number of access control policies, the overall time-consuming of the scheme does not increase, and the time-consuming of decryption can also be stabilized at about 2 s.
