KW  - privacy preserve
KW  - identity-based encryption
KW  - attribute-based encryption
KW  - PROXY RE-ENCRYPTION
KW  - PUBLIC-KEY ENCRYPTION
AB  - Micro-video sharing is prevalent nowadays due to the rapid development of personal smart devices, fast growing of network bandwidth and the easy-to-use cloud computing. However, the micro-video sharing system is more vulnerable compared to the conventional video service model because of the vulnerability of the cloud and the hardware computing constraints of personal devices. Ensuring the security and privacy of the micro-videos has become critical for micro-video sharing systems. Recently, a number of encryption schemes have been proposed to protect the security of the micro-videos stored in the cloud. However, these approaches cannot support micro-video sharing functionality. Moreover, the encryption-based method cannot provide the fine-grained access control on encrypted micro-videos. In this paper, we present a notion of fine-grained identity-based broadcast proxy re-encryption to address the issue of fine-grained encrypted micro-video sharing. Further, we present a concrete scheme in the proposed notion and proved its semantic security. Performance and evaluation reveal that our scheme is practical and efficient.
