TI  - An efficient integrity-based heterogeneous EHR data encryption and decryption framework for cloud computing environment
T2  - INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF MODELING SIMULATION AND SCIENTIFIC COMPUTING
KW  - Attribute-based encryption
KW  - cloud computing
KW  - data security
KW  - electronic health records
KW  - KEYWORD SEARCH
KW  - ACCESS-CONTROL
AB  - Cloud data security is critical in healthcare to protect patient information across diverse databases. 2D and 3D medical datasets pose challenges for traditional cloud security frameworks due to differences in format, size, and computational demands. This study introduces a hybrid encryption-decryption framework that uses token key generation for efficient distributed key management. The framework generates token keys from user-provided information, improving encryption and decryption processes. It also creates dynamic token keys to verify both homogeneous and heterogeneous data. Evaluations using 2D and 3D EHRs show that the framework outperforms traditional models in computation time and data security. These findings validate its effectiveness in securing complex datasets.
