AB  - Many organizations around the world recognize the vitality of cloud computing. However, some concerns make organizations reluctant to adopting cloud computing. These include data security, privacy, and trust issues. It is very important that these issues are addressed to meet client concerns and to encourage the wider adoption of cloud computing. This paper develops a user privacy framework based upon on emerging security model that includes access control, encryption and protection monitor schemas in the cloud environment.
